<h1>Privacy Policy — Naukri Saathi</h1>
<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 23 October 2026</p><p>Naukri Saathi helps users discover government job notifications, exam results, admit cards, study resources and related public information.</p><h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>Naukri Saathi is designed to provide public information. The information collected depends on the features enabled in the app. If you contact us, we may receive the information you voluntarily provide. Please do not submit sensitive personal information.</p><h2>2. How Information Is Used</h2>
<p>Information, where applicable, may be used to operate and improve the app, respond to user queries, maintain security and provide requested features.</p><h2>3. Storage and Sharing</h2>
<p>Some preferences or saved items may be stored on your device. Information may be processed by third-party services used by the app, if enabled. We do not claim that the app collects no data unless this has been verified.</p><h2>4. Third-Party Services and Advertising</h2>
<p>The app may link to official government websites. If advertising services such as Google AdMob are added, those services may process information under their own privacy policies. This section will be updated to accurately describe the services actually used.</p><h2>5. External Links</h2>
<p>External websites have their own privacy practices. Please review their policies before sharing information with them.</p><h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>The app is intended for a general audience seeking public education and employment information. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the app, contact us so the matter can be reviewed.</p><h2>7. Policy Updates</h2>
<p>This policy may be updated when app features or data practices change. The latest version will be published on this page.</p><h2>8. Contact</h2>
<p>For privacy questions, contact the app developer through the contact details provided on the app's official distribution page.</p>
